question:
Charlie and Dana play a game where they take turns rolling a standard die. If a player rolls $n$, they are awarded $g(n)$ points, where:
\[g(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
8 & \text{if }n\text{ is a multiple of 3}, \\
3 & \text{if }n\text{ is a prime number}, \\
1 & \text{if }n\text{ is only even (and not a multiple of 3)},
\\ 0 & \text{otherwise}.
\end{array}
\right.\]
Charlie rolls the die five times and gets the numbers 6, 4, 5, 2, and 3. Dana rolls the die four times and gets the numbers 3, 3, 1, and 2. Calculate the product of Charlie's and Dana's total points.
